The following lemma gives the decomposition of Theorem \ref{decomposition} in a special case.

\begin{proof} We prove the if part first. For a given $u\in(0,1),$ set $t=\mu(u,A).$ We have
$$\int_0^u\log(\frac{\mu(s,B)}{t})ds\leq\tau(\log_+(\frac{|B|}{t}))\leq\tau(\log_+(\frac{|A|}{t}))=\int_0^u\log(\frac{\mu(s,A)}{t})ds.$$
Hence, $B\prec\prec_{\log}A.$

We now prove the only if part. If $t>\|B\|_{\infty},$ then \eqref{eq:logAtBt} holds trivially, while if $t\le\|B\|_{\infty}$ then
we have
\begin{multline*}
\tau(\log_+(\frac{|B|}{t}))=\int_0^{d_{|B|}(t)}\log(\frac{\mu(s,B)}{t})ds\leq\int_0^{d_{|B|}(t)}\log(\frac{\mu(s,A)}{t})ds \\
\leq\int_0^{d_{|A|}(t)}\log(\frac{\mu(s,A)}{t})ds=\tau(\log_+(\frac{|A|}{t})).
\end{multline*}
\end{proof}

